{"id": "12th_tamil_mp2_q1867", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "multiple_choice", "level": "medium", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "12", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "megapack_2", "lesson_id": "grammar_poetics_masterclass", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "meyppattiyal_acham_origins", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "தொல்காப்பிய மெய்ப்பாட்டியலில் 'அச்சம்' தோன்றுவதற்குரிய நான்கு காரணங்கள் எவை?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "கல்வி, தறுகண், இசைமை, கொடை", "B": "செல்வம், புலன், புணர்வு, விளையாட்டு", "C": "அணங்கு, விலங்கு, கள்வர், இறை", "D": "மூப்பு, பிணி, வருத்தம், மென்மை"}, "explanation": "'அணங்கே விலங்கே கள்வரே இறைஎனப் பிணங்கல் சாலா அச்சம் நான்கே' என்பது தொல்காப்பிய நூற்பா (மெய்ப்பாட்டியல் 8)."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "According to Tholkappiyam, which four entities instill 'Acham' (fear/dread)?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Learning, bravery, fame, charity", "B": "Wealth, senses, union, play", "C": "Anangu (Supernatural forces/deities), Vilangu (Ferocious beasts), Kalvar (Robbers/Bandits), Irai (Oppressive rulers/kings)", "D": "Old age, sickness, sorrow, fragility"}, "explanation": "Tholkappiyar specifies supernatural spirits (Anangu), predators (Vilangu), robbers (Kalvar), and tyrants (Irai) as fear origins."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "C", "accepted_keys": ["C"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil