{"id": "12th_tamil_mp2_q1872", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "multiple_choice", "level": "medium", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "12", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "megapack_2", "lesson_id": "grammar_poetics_masterclass", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "meyppattiyal_azhugai_origins", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "தொல்காப்பிய மெய்ப்பாட்டியலில் 'அழுகை' (துன்பம்/சோகம்) தோன்றுவதற்குரிய நான்கு காரணங்கள் எவை?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "செல்வம், புலன், புணர்வு, விளையாட்டு", "B": "கல்வி, தறுகண், இசைமை, கொடை", "C": "அணங்கு, விலங்கு, கள்வர், இறை", "D": "இழிவு, இழவு, அசைவு, வறுமை"}, "explanation": "'இழிவே இழவே அசைவே வறுமையென விளிவில் கொள்கை அழுகை நான்கே' என்பது தொல்காப்பிய நூற்பா (மெய்ப்பாட்டியல் 5)."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "According to Tholkappiyam, which four calamities give rise to 'Azhugai' (weeping/sorrow)?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Wealth, senses, union, play", "B": "Learning, bravery, fame, charity", "C": "Deities, beasts, thieves, tyrants", "D": "Izhivu (Degradation), Izhavu (Bereavement/Loss), Asaivu (Helpless destitution), Varumai (Extreme poverty)"}, "explanation": "Tholkappiyar enumerates degradation, bereavement, destitution/fatigue, and acute poverty as the four causes of grief."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "D", "accepted_keys": ["D"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Tex